From cd02977688369e2549813cf8bd6cecd1bcd40988 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWCH Phase 3 <phase3@openwch.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 21:31:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] c: match WCH implicit-function diagnostics

WCH 15.2.0 keeps implicit function declarations as warnings by default in
C99 and later modes.  Use pedwarn for those modes so explicit -Werror and
-pedantic-errors still promote the diagnostic, while preserving
system-header suppression and the pre-C99 warning path.

Match the four observed WCH diagnostic literals exactly: function0 and
function1 in C99-and-later modes, and function2 and function3 before C99.
Update affected upstream expectations and add focused coverage for
severity, spelling suggestions, -fno-permissive, and system headers.

The 33-case official matrix matches return code, stdout, stderr, and
assembly byte-for-byte.  Directed tests pass; the static gcc.dg run has
37082 PASS with all 37070 baseline PASS entries retained, and the RISC-V
run retains all 30242 PASS entries of the RC01 (.highcode repair round)
baseline.  The selected EVT gate remains 274/274.

Behavior evidence:
  tmp/phase3d-t2-research/rc02/results-post-rc02
  tmp/phase3d-evidence/t2-rc02/directed-final-v6
  tmp/phase3d-evidence/t2-rc02/suite-diff-dg-final-v5
  tmp/phase3d-evidence/t2-rc02/suite-diff-riscv-final-v2

